==German==

===Etymology 1===
Old High German ''[[maska]]'', {{OS.}} [[maska]], from a Germanic root ''*maskwo(n)''.

====Noun====
'''Masche''' ''f'' (''pl'' '''Maschen''')

# a [[mesh]] (when knitting for example)

===Etymology 2===
Probably from Western Yiddish

====Noun====
'''Masche''' ''f'' (normally not used in plural)

# a [[scam]]

====Usage====
{{rfc-header|Usage}}
* ''Das ist ja ne tolle '''Masche'''.''

